  "result": "Perfect! All 202 tests pass. Here's the summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**New file: `src/statements.js`**\n- `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that generates customer account statements\n  - Returns ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })\n  - Normalizes customer ID and validates it exists (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND error)\n  - Filters invoices to only include:\n    - Matching customer\n    - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid invoices)\n    - issueDate on or before asOf (YYYY-MM-DD)\n  - Maps invoices to statement entries: { number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }\n  - Sorts by issueDate ascending\n  - Calculates totalDue as sum of individual invoice due amounts\n\n**New test file: `test/statements.test.js`**\n- 16 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Customer validation\n  - Empty statement handling\n  - Customer ID normalization\n  - Invoice filtering by status\n  - Invoice filtering by date\n  - Sorting by issueDate\n  - Payment tracking integration\n  - Mixed invoice states (issued, partially_paid, paid, draft)\n  - Statement structure validation\n\n**Updated `HANDOFF.md`**\n- Documented statement function and usage\n- Updated test counts (202 total)\n- Removed \"Invoice retrieval\" from unfinished work\n- Added statements.js to core files list\n\nAll 202 tests pass \u2713",
